# Flatmate TrustVault — environment example
#
# The default demo realm needs no environment variables: `npm run dev` starts a
# self-contained ES256 issuer and verifies every API request against it.
#
# LIVE TIDECLOAK (configuration preview — see README "Live TideCloak mode")
# The client initialises @tidecloak/js when URL + realm are set. A production
# deployment still needs the OIDC redirect/token-exchange callback and a
# remote-JWKS verifier before live credentials can replace the demo realm.
NEXT_PUBLIC_TIDECLOAK_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_TIDECLOAK_REALM=
NEXT_PUBLIC_TIDECLOAK_CLIENT_ID=flatmate-trustvault
NEXT_PUBLIC_TIDECLOAK_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:3000/auth/redirect
